    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Governance test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`): The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only in the default export. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` to `src/finetune/index.js`.\n\n2. **Eval test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`): The `toxicityMetric` function had an incompatible signature. It expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. When references were passed as banned terms, they were incorrectly flagged as toxic. I updated `toxicityMetric` to accept `(outputs, references)` and always use `defaultBannedTerms` instead.\n\n**Test results**: All 28 tests passing across 8 test files \u2713",
